I was hanging out with the cool kids in rec.games.roguelike.nethack when 
Janis Papanagnou got out a spraycan and scrawled the following:
>  While two-weaponing some artifact and a sabre a curse hit my sabre,
>  and it immediately fell off from my hand. I've never had that before
>  so I am a bit astonished about that behaviour; if a two-handed weapon
>  gets cursed you are doomed and cannot do many things, but getting your
>  second weapon cursed will release you from your problem... - why that?

Guessing, here:  With a single cursed weapon, you can carry on fighting
as normal until you find a way to uncurse it.  Your cursed off-hand
weapon slipping from your grasp means that you can't resume #twoweapon
combat (because if you wield it again, it'll weld itself to your primary
hand and you can't exchange it into the other hand), so you're suddenly
a lot less effective at killing things.

Annoying when it happens over water, but I think it still works out in
favour of #twoweaponing over weapon+shield or two-handed weapon.

